        // But the test is supposed to end with one assertion. We can do: try c.SetMinSum(0) { } catch { } then c.Collect(...) then assert MinSum.
        // However, the reference will revert on SetMinSum(0) after Initialized, so the catch will execute. Then we call Collect. In the bug, SetMinSum(0) succeeds, changing MinSum to 0. Then Collect is called. After that, MinSum in reference is 10, in bug is 0.
        // So the assertion: assertEq(c.MinSum(), 10) passes on reference (SetMinSum failed, MinSum stays 10), fails on bug (MinSum is 0). That works.
        // We need Collect to not revert. Let's make Alice's balance big enough and unlockTime past.
